2026-09-27T03:27:33.0620442Z Description:
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0620793Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0621103Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0621944Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0622885Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0622972Z Update Note
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0623190Z ===========
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0623483Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0623769Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0623860Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0624084Z ================
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0624215Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0624374Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0624753Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0624983Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0625109Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0625402Z ====================================
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0625587Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0626020Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0626554Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0626927Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0627640Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0628262Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0628394Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0628895Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0629474Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0629772Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0630098Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0630538Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0630625Z Packages
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0630821Z ========
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0630935Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0632331Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0633822Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0634041Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0634544Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0635011Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0635562Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0637677Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0638117Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0638374Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0638813Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0639053Z ==========================
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0639188Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0640241Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0705535Z 
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0706508Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0707492Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T03:27:33.0707735Z 
